# {{name}}

Lazuli `{{namespace}}` semantic scalar plugin. Pure-Go, dependency-free
validators and formatters scaffolded with `lazuli plugin new`.

## Surface

| Semantic type | Alias | Validator | Formatter |
|---|---|---|---|
| {{TypeName}}Value | `@semantic.{{TypeName}}Value` | `Validate{{TypeName}}Value` | `Format{{TypeName}}Value` |

## Install

```bash
go get {{module}}@v0.1.0
```

## Quick start

```go
package host

import {{go_package}} "{{module}}"

func ValidateField(s string) error {
	return {{go_package}}.Validate{{TypeName}}Value(s)
}
```

```toml
[plugins]
"{{namespace}}" = { module = "{{module}}", version = "v0.1.0" }
```

Edit `Validate{{TypeName}}Value` / `Format{{TypeName}}Value` with your real
rule, then add more `[[semantic_types]]` entries to `manifest.toml`.
